id: as-10-bodyguard
number: 410
name: Bodyguard
pool: Hard
description: A fields four units and does all the killing; B fields one Wardbearer and each round picks exactly one ally to stand in front of.
design: Asymmetry 10 — the widest roster gap in the batch. Four units against one.
design: Player B has a single Wardbearer whose whole turn is choosing who to cover. Guard Stance reaches the adjacent ally only, so the choice is which one — and unlike the aura it replaced, the Wardbearer takes the blow itself, so it can be staggered, shoved into a pit and killed doing the job.
retired: Its own writeup answers no and points at `as-04`. Four-versus-one is `as-01`'s question with less to do.

spawn h = Husk
spawn l = Lobber
spawn g = Grappler

roster a: Vanguard, Archer, Archer, Threadcaster
roster b: Wardbearer

